  "beats": [
    {
      "seg": "hook",
      "text": "Picture the biggest bear alive today, a full-grown grizzly, dropped into North America twenty thousand years ago.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear walking toward camera"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "glacier aerial footage"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "ice age north america megafauna paleoart"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "hook",
      "text": "The ice is a mile thick. The grass is full of giants. And every one of them is hungry.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "ice sheet glacier calving"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "mammoth steppe paleoart",
          "at": 6
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "ice age predators paleoart",
          "at": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "hook",
      "text": "Some of them would barely notice him. One of them would eat him.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "short-faced bear arctodus paleoart"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear roaring close up",
          "at": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "hook",
      "text": "Three fights. One bear. Let's see how far he gets.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bears fighting"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear standing up on hind legs",
          "at": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "title",
      "title": "Dire Wolf"
    },
    {
      "seg": "stats",
      "text": "First up, the dire wolf. It weighed around sixty kilos, noticeably heavier than a grey wolf.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "dire wolf skeleton museum"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "stats",
      "text": "Scientists have pulled more than four thousand of them out of the La Brea Tar Pits in Los Angeles.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "receipt",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dire_wolf",
          "find": "La Brea Tar Pits",
          "w": 1760,
          "h": 1100,
          "highlight": {
            "x": 0.431640625,
            "y": 0.4816193181818182,
            "w": 0.13584872159090908,
            "h": 0.03636363636363636
          },
          "src": "assets/b06-0.png",
          "credit": "en.wikipedia.org",
          "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dire_wolf"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "la brea tar pits dire wolf skull wall",
          "at": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "stats",
      "text": "That many bodies in one place tells you something. They hunted in packs.",
      "note": "Pack size is an estimate",
      "note_at": 9,
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "dire wolf pack paleoart"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "One on one, this is easy. A grizzly outweighs a single dire wolf five times over.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear walking slow motion"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "But dire wolves never came one at a time.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "wolf pack running snow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "Watch how a modern wolf pack works a bison. Nobody goes for the throat. They just keep it running until it can't.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "wolf pack hunting bison yellowstone"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "bison running from wolves",
          "at": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "A grizzly can send one wolf flying with a single swipe. The trouble is the five standing behind it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear swipe paw"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "wolves surrounding grizzly bear",
          "at": 11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "In Yellowstone, grizzlies take kills off wolf packs all the time. They walk in, and the wolves back off.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear steals wolf kill yellowstone"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "wolves back away from grizzly carcass",
          "at": 11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "tier",
      "text": "Dire wolves go in C tier. A pack could hurt him, but he walks away.",
      "tier": {
        "item": "Dire Wolf",
        "row": "C"
      }
    },
    {
      "seg": "title",
      "title": "Smilodon"
    },
    {
      "seg": "stats",
      "text": "Next, Smilodon. The North American sabre-tooth weighed up to about two hundred and eighty kilos, close to a big male grizzly.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "smilodon fatalis skeleton museum"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "smilodon fatalis paleoart",
          "at": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "stats",
      "text": "Its jaw opened to around a hundred and twenty degrees. That's how it fit those teeth around a throat.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "receipt",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smilodon",
          "find": "120",
          "w": 1760,
          "h": 1100,
          "highlight": {
            "x": 0.48190696022727275,
            "y": 0.4816193181818182,
            "w": 0.037162642045454546,
            "h": 0.03636363636363636
          },
          "src": "assets/b16-0.png",
          "credit": "en.wikipedia.org",
          "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smilodon"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "smilodon skull open jaw",
          "at": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "stats",
      "text": "And it was built heavier up front than any cat alive today, with forelimbs made for pinning prey down.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "smilodon skeleton forelimbs"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "smilodon pinning prey paleoart",
          "at": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "Here's the problem with those teeth. They were thin, and they could snap on bone.",
      "note": "Based on fossil tooth studies",
      "note_at": 7,
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "smilodon canine tooth fossil"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "So Smilodon couldn't bite a struggling bear just anywhere. It had to pin him first.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "lion pins buffalo"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "And pinning a grizzly is a nightmare. That hump on his back is solid muscle, and it powers every swing.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear digging"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear hump shoulders close",
          "at": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "Tigers do fight brown bears in Russia, and the tiger doesn't always win.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "siberian tiger snow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "Smilodon probably wins if it lands the bite first. If it doesn't, the bear breaks those teeth and the fight is over.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "smilodon attack paleoart"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear charging",
          "at": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "tier",
      "text": "Smilodon goes in A tier. On a good day for the cat, the grizzly is dead.",
      "tier": {
        "item": "Smilodon",
        "row": "A"
      }
    },
    {
      "seg": "title",
      "title": "Short-faced Bear"
    },
    {
      "seg": "stats",
      "text": "Last, the giant short-faced bear. The biggest males may have weighed around nine hundred kilos.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "arctodus simus skeleton museum"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "stats",
      "text": "On its back legs it stood over three metres tall. Your grizzly comes up to its chest.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "arctodus skeleton standing"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear standing tall",
          "at": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "stats",
      "text": "Scientists still argue about what it ate. Some think it hunted. Others think it bullied other predators off their kills.",
      "note": "Its diet is still debated",
      "note_at": 6,
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "receipt",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctodus",
          "find": "scavenger",
          "w": 1760,
          "h": 1100,
          "highlight": {
            "x": 0.4541725852272727,
            "y": 0.48267045454545454,
            "w": 0.09071377840909091,
            "h": 0.03636363636363636
          },
          "src": "assets/b27-0.png",
          "credit": "en.wikipedia.org",
          "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arctodus"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "arctodus paleoart",
          "at": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "If it was a scavenger, think about what that means. It walked up to Smilodon and took its food.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "short-faced bear paleoart scavenging"
        },
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "smilodon kill paleoart",
          "at": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "A grizzly does that to wolves today. This bear did it to everything.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear eating carcass wolves waiting"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "Our grizzly has one thing going for him. He's tough, he's low to the ground, and he fights other bears for a living.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bears fighting river"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "brown bears fighting katmai",
          "at": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "But at nine hundred kilos against three hundred, technique stops mattering.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "grizzly bear close up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "action",
      "text": "Bears settle most fights with size. The smaller bear backs off, and if it doesn't, it gets hurt.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "bear standoff river"
        },
        {
          "kind": "clip",
          "q": "bear backs away from bigger bear",
          "at": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg": "tier",
      "text": "The short-faced bear goes straight into S tier. This is the one that eats him.",
      "tier": {
        "item": "Short-faced Bear",
        "row": "S"
      }
    },
    {
      "seg": "wheel",
      "text": "Bonus round. The wheel picks who he fights next.",
      "wheel": {
        "names": [
          "Cave Lion",
          "Woolly Rhino",
          "Cave Hyena",
          "Ground Sloth",
          "Mammoth",
          "Megalania"
        ],
        "pick": "Cave Lion"
      }
    },
    {
      "seg": "outro",
      "text": "The cave lion. That fight is next.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "kind": "image",
          "q": "cave lion paleoart"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
